# `s = raw"a\b"` - a raw string, where `\b` is two literal bytes.
#
# `lacks escape_sequence` is the whole point of this specimen. julia.json
# gives prefixed_string_literal its own content terminals - the `_raw`
# variants - precisely because a prefixed literal does not take escapes, so a
# hand that reuses the ordinary string interior here emits an escape_sequence
# node over bytes that are not one. That is a wrong shape rather than a
# missing one, and no byte measurement would notice it.
roots 1
mends 0
holds prefixed_string_literal
lacks escape_sequence
spans prefixed_string_literal 4 12
